1336
01:00:50.880 --> 01:00:52.360
And he just sort of starts stammering.

1337
01:00:52.480 --> 01:00:55.280
And he just keeps introducing himself over and over again.

1338
01:00:55.440 --> 01:00:55.740
Hi.

1339
01:00:56.160 --> 01:00:56.560
Hi.

1340
01:00:56.960 --> 01:00:57.360
Hi.

1341
01:00:57.420 --> 01:00:57.820
Hi.

1342
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:58.250
Hi.

1343
01:00:58.250 --> 01:00:58.580
Hi.

1344
01:00:58.580 --> 01:01:01.320
And I love that Stanley's like, I'm not helping you.

1345
01:01:01.420 --> 01:01:02.740
In fact, I'm just going to ignore you.

1346
01:01:02.740 --> 01:01:09.020
I'm going to turn away and do my crossword and let you just, what's the expression to

1347
01:01:09.020 --> 01:01:10.380
know where it just, you flap in the wind.

1348
01:01:10.400 --> 01:01:11.040
Blow in the wind.

1349
01:01:11.660 --> 01:01:12.020
Yeah.

1350
01:01:12.160 --> 01:01:12.940
Something like that.

1351
01:01:13.080 --> 01:01:15.160
He's just going to hang them out to dry there.

1352
01:01:15.240 --> 01:01:15.920
It's so good.

1353
01:01:16.260 --> 01:01:19.480
I was able to find out the names of two of the clients, but I couldn't find names for

1354
01:01:19.480 --> 01:01:20.160
the other guys.

1355
01:01:20.280 --> 01:01:21.340
But Landon H.

1356
01:01:21.440 --> 01:01:21.980
Lewis Jr.

1357
01:01:22.340 --> 01:01:23.660
and Leon Simmons Jr.

1358
01:01:23.960 --> 01:01:26.840
are two of the clients in that scene.

1359
01:01:27.060 --> 01:01:32.220
I also loved how all of the men in the scene were so much taller than BJ.

1360
01:01:32.940 --> 01:01:33.460
Yes.

1361
01:01:33.640 --> 01:01:38.160
Because it really also made him just look so young, you know?

1362
01:01:38.500 --> 01:01:38.680
Yeah.

1363
01:01:39.020 --> 01:01:39.880
Next to them.

1364
01:01:40.200 --> 01:01:41.360
Just the size difference.

1365
01:01:42.260 --> 01:01:42.700
Yes.

1366
01:01:42.880 --> 01:01:48.140
And then later when they're in the car, Angela, Stanley cannot stop laughing.

1367
01:01:48.400 --> 01:01:52.540
There are all these shots that go back to them driving back to Dunder Mifflin.

1368
01:01:52.900 --> 01:01:56.480
And Stanley is just like, can't believe.

1369
01:01:56.480 --> 01:01:58.480
He's so delighted by how that went.

1370
01:01:58.720 --> 01:01:59.680
He's so tickled.

1371
01:01:59.820 --> 01:02:01.160
It clearly made his day.

1372
01:02:01.160 --> 01:02:05.560
I don't know that Stanley gets much joy out of working at Dunder Mifflin, but this was

1373
01:02:05.560 --> 01:02:07.020
a real highlight for him.

1374
01:02:07.340 --> 01:02:10.740
And there's this moment that Leslie talks about in the DVD.

1375
01:02:11.080 --> 01:02:16.180
He said in the script, it was just that Stanley is driving and laughing and they just kind of

1376
01:02:16.180 --> 01:02:16.960
let him go.

1377
01:02:17.040 --> 01:02:22.480
And he improvised the whole thing about, hi, hi, you sounded like my six-month-old niece.

1378
01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:24.740
And like all of that, Leslie was just riffing.

1379
01:02:24.740 --> 01:02:27.040
Oh, that was so good.

1380
01:02:27.340 --> 01:02:28.080
I know.

1381
01:02:28.200 --> 01:02:34.340
And he said, in fact, whenever Stanley would go off on Ryan, as he has throughout the show,

1382
01:02:34.680 --> 01:02:37.360
they would just let Leslie just go.

1383
01:02:37.560 --> 01:02:39.800
And I think there's some amazing moments.

1384
01:02:40.220 --> 01:02:41.300
Oh, yes.

1385
01:02:41.480 --> 01:02:41.860
Yes.

1386
01:02:42.300 --> 01:02:47.260
Well, you know, and this is Ryan's second sales call now that has not gone well.

1387
01:02:47.260 --> 01:02:50.300
Remember, he went on the initiation sales call with Dwight.

1388
01:02:50.440 --> 01:02:51.700
They did not make the sale.

1389
01:02:51.840 --> 01:02:54.400
And now he's gone out on this call with Stanley.

1390
01:02:54.540 --> 01:02:56.820
Now, I believe Stanley's going to save this sale.

1391
01:02:57.180 --> 01:02:58.540
Oh, Stanley for sure saved it.

1392
01:02:58.760 --> 01:02:58.960
Okay.

1393
01:02:59.080 --> 01:03:03.880
So while all of these sales meetings are happening, Pam and Angela are at the coffee shop.

1394
01:03:04.260 --> 01:03:06.400
Angela is in such a great mood.

1395
01:03:06.400 --> 01:03:14.060
And she's telling Pam a story about how she had this friend who was in need and this gallant

1396
01:03:14.060 --> 01:03:15.680
man came to her rescue.

1397
01:03:16.120 --> 01:03:16.460
Yeah.

1398
01:03:16.640 --> 01:03:23.280
She's like, he must really care for her a lot because he did this wonderful thing for my

1399
01:03:23.280 --> 01:03:23.840
friend.

1400
01:03:24.300 --> 01:03:24.740
Yeah.

1401
01:03:24.900 --> 01:03:26.160
She's talking in code.

1402
01:03:26.780 --> 01:03:28.100
She's speaking in code.

1403
01:03:28.300 --> 01:03:31.240
She's like, my friend, let's call her Noel.

1404
01:03:31.840 --> 01:03:35.040
And this gallant gentleman, we'll call him Kurt.

1405
01:03:35.040 --> 01:03:40.620
Well, we all know that Kurt is Dwight's middle name, right?

1406
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:41.280
Yes.

1407
01:03:41.440 --> 01:03:43.940
And we got a lot of fan questions about this, Angela.

1408
01:03:44.520 --> 01:03:52.460
Kenzie B., Elizabeth R., Julia Lee, Nicole Fink, and Katie Krull all want to know when

1409
01:03:52.460 --> 01:04:00.200
Angela refers to her friend Noel, is that because Noel is Angela's middle name?

1410
01:04:01.180 --> 01:04:05.020
It definitely sounds like a very Angela Martin middle name.

1411
01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:08.500
Well, yes, it is Angela's middle name.

1412
01:04:08.700 --> 01:04:13.460
Angela thinks she's being really savvy, but Pam totally knows who she's talking about.

1413
01:04:13.780 --> 01:04:15.780
But yes, that is her middle name.

1414
01:04:15.880 --> 01:04:17.720
But Jenna, I have a question for you.

1415
01:04:18.480 --> 01:04:19.000
Okay.

1416
01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:21.020
Is Noel in the script?

1417
01:04:21.080 --> 01:04:23.460
Because I have a little story about that middle name.

1418
01:04:23.560 --> 01:04:24.180
And I'm curious.

1419
01:04:24.780 --> 01:04:27.580
I think what was in the script was Colette.

1420
01:04:28.540 --> 01:04:35.860
Okay, I looked this up and in the script, Angela actually says this.

1421
01:04:36.080 --> 01:04:42.320
She says, well, a friend of mine, let's just call her, oh, let's just call her me.

1422
01:04:42.860 --> 01:04:43.500
What?

1423
01:04:43.740 --> 01:04:44.720
And then you giggle.

1424
01:04:45.780 --> 01:04:52.200
Okay, so my memory of this is when we were shooting it that day, that the writers were

1425
01:04:52.200 --> 01:04:55.460
pitching me different middle names, like different things to say.

1426
01:04:55.640 --> 01:04:57.880
I know in one of them it was Colette.

1427
01:04:58.040 --> 01:04:59.760
I have such a memory of saying that.

1428
01:05:01.040 --> 01:05:03.060
And then we said Noel.

1429
01:05:03.340 --> 01:05:08.920
And I like Noel the best because it sounds very sort of Angela Martin, doesn't it?

1430
01:05:08.920 --> 01:05:15.620
It's her love of Christmas, her love of the story of Christmas, that Noel would be her middle

1431
01:05:15.620 --> 01:05:16.100
name.

1432
01:05:16.920 --> 01:05:18.740
And that's the one we went with.

1433
01:05:19.120 --> 01:05:21.580
And Dave Rogers talks about it in the DVD commentary.

1434
01:05:21.580 --> 01:05:25.100
And he goes, I remember it being Colette.

1435
01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:29.180
And he thought maybe I improvised Noel, but I didn't.

1436
01:05:29.320 --> 01:05:30.320
That was a writer's pitch.

1437
01:05:30.620 --> 01:05:32.340
I mean, I think I was part of the dialogue.

1438
01:05:32.520 --> 01:05:33.780
I think we were pitching names.

1439
01:05:33.780 --> 01:05:36.280
But that all sort of happened in the moment.

1440
01:05:36.620 --> 01:05:37.560
I love it.

1441
01:05:37.720 --> 01:05:38.800
It's perfect.

1442
01:05:39.380 --> 01:05:42.600
It is such Angela Noel Martin.

1443
01:05:42.860 --> 01:05:46.120
And I believe that will appear on your wedding invitation.

1444
01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:47.260
Oh, yeah.

1445
01:05:47.520 --> 01:05:50.540
It's now part of my character's show Bible.

1446
01:05:51.280 --> 01:05:54.900
We had another fan catch in this scene, Angela.

1447
01:05:55.160 --> 01:05:59.660
Sarah Rouse wrote in to say, Pam is holding a piece of paper at the coffee shop.

1448
01:05:59.680 --> 01:06:01.360
What is that supposed to be?

1449
01:06:01.420 --> 01:06:02.400
And what does it say?

1450
01:06:02.400 --> 01:06:09.160
Okay, well, Sarah, that was the list of coffee orders from those deleted scenes.

1451
01:06:09.660 --> 01:06:13.540
I had all the coffee orders written down on that piece of paper, and I was going to use

1452
01:06:13.540 --> 01:06:14.460
it to make my order.

1453
01:06:14.720 --> 01:06:21.080
Well, Angela, also in this scene, just because we were talking about it earlier, your flower

1454
01:06:21.080 --> 01:06:23.560
hairdo is on full display.

1455
01:06:23.760 --> 01:06:30.900
Just if you really want some great shots of it, guys, here it is, her WTF hairdo right

1456
01:06:30.900 --> 01:06:31.160
here.

1457
01:06:31.500 --> 01:06:32.020
WTF.

1458
01:06:32.020 --> 01:06:32.940
Well, wait, wait.

1459
01:06:33.040 --> 01:06:33.880
I have something to share.

1460
01:06:34.060 --> 01:06:39.720
So while we were on a break, I had been texting Kim Ferry about this hair, and she texted back.

1461
01:06:39.860 --> 01:06:42.060
And so this is what she had to say about it.

1462
01:06:42.260 --> 01:06:44.860
I said, oh my gosh, it's a real-time tidbit.

1463
01:06:45.040 --> 01:06:46.220
It's a real-time tidbit.

1464
01:06:46.220 --> 01:06:47.780
It just came in a few minutes ago.

1465
01:06:48.580 --> 01:06:53.340
I said, Kim, what was the inspiration for this bun?

1466
01:06:53.340 --> 01:06:58.100
I mean, I know that we thought my character was going to, like, be in a great mood, and

1467
01:06:58.100 --> 01:06:59.680
so we wanted to try something new.

1468
01:06:59.720 --> 01:07:00.860
She said, yes.

1469
01:07:00.860 --> 01:07:02.740
Here is the inspiration.

1470
01:07:02.740 --> 01:07:09.480
She said, my first job in the business was working on a sci-fi show called Babylon 5.

1471
01:07:09.480 --> 01:07:16.880
I worked on this show for five years, and I couldn't use any contemporary hairstyles because

1472
01:07:16.880 --> 01:07:19.300
they wanted the hairstyles to look futuristic.

1473
01:07:19.300 --> 01:07:26.320
So I started coming up with all these different kind of braids and buns with wires and fancy

1474
01:07:26.320 --> 01:07:31.360
updos and Zulu knots, basically anything different that I could think of.

1475
01:07:31.360 --> 01:07:39.180
And your bun with those fun swirls was a good one for me because I had done it on Babylon 5.

1476
01:07:39.500 --> 01:07:44.580
It's fast and easy, but technically, this is a sci-fi hairstyle.

1477
01:07:45.080 --> 01:07:48.060
Oh my gosh.

1478
01:07:48.320 --> 01:07:49.520
Isn't that great?

1479
01:07:50.520 --> 01:07:54.380
Don't you feel like Dwight would have loved it because he was Mr. Sci-Fi?

1480
01:07:55.320 --> 01:07:55.960
Yes.

1481
01:07:56.520 --> 01:07:57.120
Yes.

1482
01:07:57.120 --> 01:08:00.660
No wonder she did her hair in this Babylon 5 hairstyle.

1483
01:08:01.360 --> 01:08:04.560
To thank Dwight for his, like, favor.

1484
01:08:04.980 --> 01:08:05.580
Yeah.

1485
01:08:05.820 --> 01:08:11.200
So yes, this hairstyle inspired by Babylon 5, it's the sci-fi bun.

1486
01:08:12.740 --> 01:08:14.560
I don't think I could love that more.

1487
01:08:15.040 --> 01:08:17.140
Kim Ferry, thank you for the real-time tidbit.

1488
01:08:17.480 --> 01:08:18.460
Thank you, Kim Ferry.

1489
01:08:19.060 --> 01:08:22.140
Sam just wrote, beats Bears Babylon 5.

1490
01:08:23.360 --> 01:08:24.820
Beats, oh wait, here we go.

1491
01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:27.660
Bears beats Babylon 5 buns.

1492
01:08:28.060 --> 01:08:28.380
Oh.

1493
01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:33.260
Okay, so now everybody is coming back from their sales calls.

1494
01:08:33.540 --> 01:08:34.280
Everyone's done.

1495
01:08:34.540 --> 01:08:39.720
And we have this amazing scene in the car with Karen and Phyllis.

1496
01:08:40.520 --> 01:08:47.520
Phyllis is so good in this scene because, you guys, she is going to reveal such a big plot point

1497
01:08:47.520 --> 01:08:50.260
and she just throws it away, right?

1498
01:08:50.620 --> 01:08:53.240
It's not, like, belabored in any way.

1499
01:08:53.280 --> 01:08:55.200
It's so perfect.

1500
01:08:56.080 --> 01:08:56.640
Yeah.

1501
01:08:57.020 --> 01:09:00.540
She's like, Karen, I had a lot of fun with you today.

1502
01:09:00.600 --> 01:09:02.460
I really enjoy spending time with you.

1503
01:09:02.600 --> 01:09:03.480
They're bonding.

1504
01:09:03.480 --> 01:09:04.640
They feel good.

1505
01:09:05.040 --> 01:09:10.460
And then she just very offhandedly says, and I'm really glad you're with Jim.

1506
01:09:10.460 --> 01:09:16.520
It makes me really happy because, you know, he was really hung up on Pam for such a long time.

1507
01:09:16.840 --> 01:09:18.820
And she's not even looking at Karen.

1508
01:09:18.980 --> 01:09:20.380
She's looking in a rearview mirror.

1509
01:09:20.540 --> 01:09:21.100
She's turning.

1510
01:09:21.300 --> 01:09:21.940
She's just driving.

1511
01:09:22.160 --> 01:09:24.260
She's sort of saying something off the cuff.

1512
01:09:24.440 --> 01:09:24.880
Yeah.

1513
01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:26.160
And it's that much more powerful.

1514
01:09:26.160 --> 01:09:32.080
And then Rashida, oh, my gosh, her reaction is so perfect.

1515
01:09:33.020 --> 01:09:34.880
It's a fantastic scene.

1516
01:09:35.080 --> 01:09:36.020
Fantastic scene.

1517
01:09:36.620 --> 01:09:39.780
I feel like her pulse stops for a second.

1518
01:09:39.940 --> 01:09:43.560
Like, I feel like I can see the wind go out of her, right?

